# IBKR Integration

Full reference: `docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`

## Ports

- Paper Gateway: `IBKR_PAPER_PORT=4002` (not TWS 7497)
- Live: `IBKR_PORT=7496` or Gateway 4001
- Host: `IBKR_HOST=127.0.0.1` (or `ib-gateway` in Docker Compose)

## Client IDs

- Broker execution: `IBKR_CLIENT_ID` (default 1)
- Data provider (`build_live_providers`): `client_id=2` — keep separate

## Threading (critical)

- `connect()` must run on a thread that owns the ib_async event loop
- Subscribe once in `connect()`: `reqAccountSummary`, `qualifyContracts`, `reqContractDetails` (SPY)
- `is_market_open()` reads cached `_market_hours_details` — safe from any thread after connect
- Calling ib_async async methods from APScheduler or random FastAPI threads **hangs forever**

## Market data type

- Default `market_data_type=3` (delayed) — paper accounts often lack live subscriptions

## Auto-start

- Never call `connect()` from FastAPI lifespan directly — use `asyncio.to_thread(bootstrap_live_from_yaml)`

## Data farm outages (fail fast, don't retry blind)

- IBKR's Gateway proactively reports HMDS (historical-data) farm health via
  `errorEvent` codes 2105 (broken) / 2106 (OK) / 2107 (inactive but
  available on demand — treat as fine). `IBKRBroker._on_ib_error` (wired in
  `connect()`) tracks this; query it via `is_historical_data_farm_broken()`.
- `IBKRProvider._get_prices` checks this before its per-symbol
  `reqHistoricalData` loop (and again after the first failure) and bails
  immediately instead of retrying every symbol out to its own timeout.
  Confirmed live 2026-09-23: a broken `ushmds` farm cost ~8 minutes proving
  the same outage 25 times before this fix.
- Only applies when a `shared_broker` is set — a private `IBKRProvider`
  connection has no equivalent tracking.
